  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Spirit Affinity House she calls the move’s name while training inside a Gu formation. The light flies into the sky and vanishes. The pale white formation space darkens. Meteors rain on a hill-like desolate beast tortoise that retracts into its shell. Fragments burst from the shell. Remaining meteors dig huge pits around the tortoise. The fall lasts twenty breaths of time. She is covered in sweat and breathing roughly. A voice from the formation says she is already proficient and tells her to train her defensive killer move next. Heavenly Court chose this move for her as powerful, easy to control, using few Gu worms, with simple activation steps.",
      "chapters": [
        1234
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_spirit_affinity_house",
        "sys_gu_formation",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Against Zhao Pu she activates it again. A patch of deep blue forms above the hall dome. Countless thin, small meteors fall like hidden weapons, a storm that cannot be avoided. Zhao Pu raises a large bloody cloud like an umbrella. The meteors shrink that cloud at a visible speed, and he has to replenish it. This move and life locking silver chain are the two she has practised the most.",
      "chapters": [
        1262
      ],
